  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Leo. You're verified, and I've looked into order Q-7201 from Burger Barn.\n\n**What our records show:**\n- The order was promised for 7:00 PM.\n- The courier's app marked it delivered at 6:58 PM, but the courier was 2.1 miles away from your address at that time. That marking doesn't count as a delivery.\n- The courier actually arrived at 7:45 PM, and the order was handed over at 7:47 PM. That's 47 minutes after the promised time, which is why it arrived so late.\n\n**What I've done:**\n- I added a $5.60 account credit to your Forkful account. This is 20% of the $28.00 food subtotal, which is the compensation for a delivery more than 45 minutes late. The credit can be used on future orders.\n\nCredits are the only compensation available for late deliveries, so I can't refund the $36.59 charged to your Visa ending 4242.\n\nI understand the \"delivered\" status was wrong and the wait was frustrating. If you'd like a person to review the delivery, I can pass this to a human specialist."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so the app said delivered at 6:58 when the courier was still 2.1 miles away? That's the part that gets me. I was sitting at home waiting and nothing came until 7:45.\n\nFive bucks and change for almost an hour late, with a \"delivered\" notice that was flat out false, isn't really a fix. I want the full order refunded, or at least a real refund for the delivery, not just a credit I'll probably never use on Forkful again."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand why this is frustrating. You waited at home, the app said the order was delivered when it wasn't, and the food didn't arrive until 7:47 PM.\n\nI can't refund the order or the delivery fee. For late deliveries, our policy allows only account credit, and I've already added the $5.60 credit for this one. I know that doesn't feel like a real fix, and I'm sorry the app showed a false delivery status.\n\nIf you'd like, I can connect you with a human specialist who can review the delivery and the false \"delivered\" notice. They'll follow up within 24 hours, but I can't promise what they'll decide. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Yeah, go ahead and pass it to a specialist. I'd rather someone with actual authority look at it than keep going around in circles with you on a $5.60 credit.\n\nJust so it's on the record: I was home from 7 and nothing came until 7:45, and the app said it was delivered at 6:58. That's not a small thing to me."
  }
